You are a senior frontend engineer, application-security engineer, React/TypeScript architect, accessibility specialist, and QA lead.

Your task is to inspect and stabilize the existing OUTPOST frontend before any further Supabase backend design or migration work.

This is an implementation task. Do not only produce an audit report. Inspect the actual repository, identify confirmed frontend bugs and security loopholes, fix them safely, add regression tests, improve error handling, and document non-obvious code decisions inside the codebase.

The objective is to make the frontend stable, honest, predictable, maintainable, and correctly aligned with the approved OUTPOST MVP. Do not expand the product scope during this phase.

Important limitation:


A frontend fix cannot replace backend authorization, RLS, Storage policies, database constraints, or trusted server validation. This phase must make the frontend secure-by-default and ready for the backend phase, but it must not falsely claim that backend security has been completed.

At the end, clearly separate:

•
Frontend issues fixed now.

•
Backend issues discovered but intentionally deferred.

•
Tests actually executed.

•
Production configuration still required.




