2. MVP CROSS-CHECK RULES

Use these rules when deciding whether a feature is a bug, an out-of-scope feature, or a backend dependency.

1.
Dambare and Rimin Gata are the case-study locations.

2.
Listings must not appear publicly unless the frontend receives them as approved/visible records.

3.
Exact landlord/property coordinates must not be exposed before location verification.

4.
Student device coordinates are temporary by default and must not be stored as movement history.

5.
Student verification is not equivalent to email verification.

6.
Landlord verification is not equivalent to property approval.

7.
Property approval is not equivalent to location approval.

8.
A reservation hold is not a confirmed payment.

9.
Receipt upload is not receipt approval.

10.
UI route protection is not backend authorization.

11.
Client-side filtering is not database access control.

12.
Local cache data is not authoritative production data.

13.
A passing TypeScript build does not prove that the feature works against the real schema.

14.
A passing static security test does not prove that live RLS or Storage policies work.

15.
Map functionality must not block the textual address/directions discovery flow if the MVP documentation identifies map rendering as a later enhancement.

16.
No frontend fallback may invent a successful result after a backend failure.

17.
No frontend fallback may create fake financial, reservation, verification, or identity records.




